<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:51Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Can Hichilema heal Zambia's political divide?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a160310c729b86abf5bf4d02f1e58a439a2f02118c86edb164ab1d7811d96906</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-hichilema-heal-zambia-s-political-divide/a-78876039--19013021f70f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-hichilema-heal-zambia-s-political-divide/a-78876039?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Zambian president starts a second term after a contested election exposed deep political divisions. His challenge now is to unite the country while addressing concerns over political freedoms.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa airline behind viral stadium flyby scraps repeat display</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9aa720147e9a769596996970f75d9f49d5d4d48e82a170cfa62086b8ec544d26</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:22:51Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-airline-behind-viral-stadium-flyby-scraps-repeat-display/a-78870028--69daa320153e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-airline-behind-viral-stadium-flyby-scraps-repeat-display/a-78870028?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two passenger jets passed close to Cape Town's DHL Stadium during a flyover last weekend. The carrier said it has shelved plans to repeat the display as South Africa's aviation authority investigates the event.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: Tens of thousands rally over Ceuta crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4909723263e944855efd52b4a0fc8479a6cacfbcdfd2d4c8c0ad91c381a46a25</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T23:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-tens-of-thousands-rally-over-ceuta-crisis/a-78814756--b0db1adff664.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-tens-of-thousands-rally-over-ceuta-crisis/a-78814756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tensions continue over migrants still stranded in Ceuta and the Sanchez government’s handling of the fallout.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Armed men abduct Kenyan editor, employer suspects government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7542e95b595c1b9fd4ca61c448a16527e9e66282089f768d53fc3c6d8757c3b</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T12:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/armed-men-abduct-kenyan-editor-employer-suspects-government/a-78721264--899ed2a0bd47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/armed-men-abduct-kenyan-editor-employer-suspects-government/a-78721264?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A newspaper editor in Kenya was kidnapped from a car late on Tuesday and then located near a dam far away a few hours later. The Standard paper said it suspected state involvement in an attempt to intimidate reporters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tunisia's activists decry civil society crackdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45b2aa639ae75339b259812c6a3d61b0271114ccefb8a98c03c0366d76e07db4</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T04:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tunisia-s-activists-decry-civil-society-crackdown/a-78614966--e657463dce69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tunisia-s-activists-decry-civil-society-crackdown/a-78614966?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Five years into Tunisian President Kais Saied’s increasingly authoritarian rule, rights groups warn that the country’s once vibrant civil society is being silenced.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Congo's Ebola caseload tops 6,000 as concerns grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b159f65ace57a8ff417fe8c57819bf0501cd173a945fc4562a47e786ceeb4de0</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:47Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447--5f990f71c7d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/congo-s-ebola-caseload-tops-6-000-as-concerns-grow/a-78638447?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo has surpassed 6,000 confirmed cases, with nearly 3,000 deaths. As the virus spreads, authorities are racing to contain one of the deadliest outbreaks in history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Amanal Petros: From refugee to European champion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f6538eb7b83854331338a9752adad5869883d6921e2dc07dc39f80c517ef46b</id><updated>2026-09-03T19:20:47Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T11:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504--a9305ea94714.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/amanal-petros-from-refugee-to-european-champion/a-78428504?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amanal Petros fled the Eritrean–Ethiopian war and came to Germany as a teenager. Now one of the world's top marathon runners, he recently won gold at the European Athletics Championships.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry></feed>
